  "atomic_questions": [
    "The delay compensation is charged per unit per quarter of delay — does this mean that if a unit is produced in quarter t and delivered in quarter t+k (k≥1), the penalty is k times the per-quarter rate (i.e., it accumulates each quarter the unit sits in inventory), or is it a flat one-time penalty equal to one quarter's rate regardless of how many quarters late the delivery is?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive interpretations of how the delay penalty is calculated."
}

